# Documentation language: ASD-STE100

Unless the user explicitly asks for another language or style, write and update **all documentation** in **ASD Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100)**.

Applies to: `README*`, `docs/**`, `**/*.md`, example/demo copy that acts as docs, and any new doc the agent creates.

## STE writing rules

- Prefer short sentences (about one idea each).
- Use active voice and simple, common words.
- Prefer present tense for facts; use imperative for procedures.
- Keep approved domain nouns (`provider`, `locator`, `flush`, API names) when needed.
- Avoid Chinese unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not invent jargon; keep meaning faithful to the source.

## Examples

```markdown
<!-- ❌ Avoid -->
本协议旨在统一多后端对象存储的抽象，并尽可能覆盖各类边界情况。

<!-- ✅ Prefer -->
This SDK gives one API for object storage on many backends.
```

```markdown
<!-- ❌ Avoid -->
Callers should endeavor to ensure configuration validity prior to invocation.

<!-- ✅ Prefer -->
Check the config before you call the API.
```
